  "segments": [
    {
      "idx": 0,
      "start_ms": 8000,
      "end_ms": 15000,
      "speaker": "Andrew Huberman",
      "text": "Why do so many people experience severe brain fog at 2 PM?"
    },
    {
      "idx": 1,
      "start_ms": 15200,
      "end_ms": 24000,
      "speaker": "Andrew Huberman",
      "text": "It comes down to adenosine buildup and circadian temperature fluctuations."
    },
    {
      "idx": 2,
      "start_ms": 24200,
      "end_ms": 37000,
      "speaker": "Andrew Huberman",
      "text": "If you view bright sunlight within 30 minutes of waking up, you trigger a cortisol pulse that sets your internal clock."
    },
    {
      "idx": 3,
      "start_ms": 37200,
      "end_ms": 48000,
      "speaker": "Andrew Huberman",
      "text": "This single habit boosts afternoon alertness more than an extra cup of coffee."
    },
    {
      "idx": 4,
      "start_ms": 48200,
      "end_ms": 56000,
      "speaker": "Andrew Huberman",
      "text": "And that is how you sustain deep focus without energy crashes."
    },
    {
      "idx": 5,
      "start_ms": 65000,
      "end_ms": 72000,
      "speaker": "Host",
      "text": "Okay, let us look at the temperature logs from lab experiment four."
    },
    {
      "idx": 6,
      "start_ms": 72200,
      "end_ms": 79000,
      "speaker": "Host",
      "text": "We recorded room temperature at twenty-two degrees celsius."
    },
    {
      "idx": 7,
      "start_ms": 180000,
      "end_ms": 188000,
      "speaker": "Andrew Huberman",
      "text": "The biggest mistake people make with dopamine is stacking too many rewards at once."
    },
    {
      "idx": 8,
      "start_ms": 188200,
      "end_ms": 199000,
      "speaker": "Andrew Huberman",
      "text": "When you listen to upbeat music while drinking pre-workout while talking to friends, your dopamine peaks enormously."
    },
    {
      "idx": 9,
      "start_ms": 199200,
      "end_ms": 209000,
      "speaker": "Andrew Huberman",
      "text": "The problem is the ensuing crash drops your baseline lower than where you started."
    },
    {
      "idx": 10,
      "start_ms": 209200,
      "end_ms": 220000,
      "speaker": "Andrew Huberman",
      "text": "To maintain intrinsic motivation, you must learn to attach dopamine release to the effort itself."
    }
  ],
